{"skill":{"slug":"requesting-code-review","displayName":"Requesting Code Review"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770691916262,"changelog":"Initial release: 请求代码审查","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2700,"sha256":"2da31af22a58938ab78f3ee6d5b4687fcca062b923b646459eb52ba72117ef97","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"code-reviewer.md","size":3385,"sha256":"7f5328dca12cb200005ae9d4386f63a9b0acb735ece57f82db206b4a3189ccae","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1867,"sha256":"c51ce1d407001b382579d4a2e0f39db518b1c2a798b5861c63b3b9d2a14d3ee4","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789056667377,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a45416ddef91bda05f68bd637e8fd67ed9d26e4f06c82fb01a31ee530040de03","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a45416ddef91bda05f68bd637e8fd67ed9d26e4f06c82fb01a31ee530040de03","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: requesting-code-review\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to facilitate code reviews by an AI agent. All instructions in SKILL.md and code-reviewer.md, including the use of `git` commands (`git rev-parse`, `git log`, `git diff`), are directly related to gathering information for and performing a code review. These `git` commands are read-only and do not pose a security risk. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's purpose, or obfuscation. The content is clearly aligned with its stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162653861},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":16,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789056667377},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a code-review workflow helper and does not show evidence of hidden execution, persistence, credential access, or data exfiltration.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill asks for local git metadata and diffs and dispatches a review subagent; repository-code exposure is expected for code review and there is no evidence of unrelated local indexing, credential use, or network transfer.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact contains Markdown instructions only, with no installer scripts, executable payloads, external dependencies, or remote retrieval behavior.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The activation guidance is broad and mandatory at common development milestones, which may cause more frequent reviews, but it is disclosed and still aligned with the workflow rather than hidden or deceptive.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No artifact instructions create persistence, modify system configuration, escalate privileges, write memory, install hooks, or use credentials.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifacts coherently support requesting a code-review subagent, collecting git SHAs, reviewing a diff, and categorizing review findings; these capabilities fit the stated code-review purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this if you want the agent to proactively request code reviews during development. Expect it to inspect git diffs and share them with a review subagent; review frequency may be higher than you want unless you tune or override the workflow.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad trigger language is real, but it is visible workflow guidance for requesting reviews around task completion and merges; it is a scope/usability note, not a material security concern by itself.\n[EA2] expected: The cited phrase tells the reviewer not to approve code without checking it; the artifact does not authorize destructive operations, financial actions, data deletion, or other high-impact autonomous actions.\n[aig-skill-scan] expected: The supplied static scan reported no results, which is consistent with the inspected Markdown-only artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789056667377}}}}}